title: 'v7.1 round 4: closed the notebook loop + promotion instrument (belief-delta gate deferred)'
summary: 'Fourth v7.x fast-follow, reshaped by adversarial review. The belief-delta promotion gate was DESIGNED (Loid) then ADVERSARIALLY REVIEWED (Jinx) — and deferred: Jinx proved it unfalsifiable (nothing measures promotion correctness, so the bands can''t be calibrated) and that the max() ratchet structurally prevents downward belief revision. Instead v7.1 shipped the sound prerequisites: (1) fixed a real open-loop bug — addNotebookEntry never persisted confidence; promotion now writes confidence_after (no ratchet); (2) a promotion-decisions.jsonl instrument logging {before(real notebook prior), after, delta, promoted, priorFound} per decision, while the proven absolute≥0.8 gate runs UNCHANGED (regression-locked by test). Caught + fixed a variable-shadow bug in the builder''s instrument code (a local `promoted` boolean shadowed the accumulator array → threw). Build clean; mcp 385→397.'
symbols_touched:
  - '#nomination-engine'
  - '#notebook-loader'
learnings:
  - 'The adversarial review paid off AGAIN — and the meta-lesson is the v7 thesis itself: the belief-delta gate would have shipped an UNFALSIFIABLE check (the exact thing v7 exists to kill). Jinx caught that the floor (after>=0.7) swallowed the delta math on the majority no-prior path (reducing to a 0.8→0.7 nerf), the four bands had no calibration signal, and the max() ratchet made beliefs un-revisable downward. Right move: ship the measurement first, build the gate from data later.'
  - Loid's own §5 self-critique was strong but did NOT substitute for an independent adversary — Jinx found the ratchet-breaks-downward-revision KILL that Loid had rationalized as a feature (can't lower a curated belief). Don't let one agent's self-review close the loop; that's 'consensus recorded as rigor'.
  - Builder cut off mid-debug with 5 failing tests; root cause was a one-line variable shadow (instrument's `const promoted` boolean shadowed the `promoted` accumulator array → promoted.push threw). Verifying state directly (run the failing test, read the diff) found it in minutes — don't trust a truncated builder report.
